<p>fMRI Study Check · Separate overnight follow-up</p><h1>How does regional support vary across sides?</h1>
<p>Eight original adults, two existing Harvard–Oxford atlas regions (14 and 37), and three supplied-coordinate strata: left, midline and right. This audit stratifies existing voxel centers; it does not replace the primary atlas, estimate a new registration or calculate connectivity.</p>
<div class="note">Independent SPM8 mask overlap and tutorial temporal variation are different evidence layers with different denominators. Neither certifies biological signal. The exact matching 2019 fMRIPrep parent data, mask and preprocessing report remain unavailable. All existing sources, results and the sealed coverage audit are preserved.</div>
<h2>Actual left/right findings</h2><img src="{{ figure }}" alt="Eight participants, left and right: independent mask overlap and tutorial varying-center fraction plotted separately for regions 14 and 37 on fixed zero-to-one-hundred percent scales">
<p>Regions retain their original IDs: 14, Inferior Temporal Gyrus, anterior division; 37, Temporal Fusiform Cortex, anterior division. All acquired frames are used. The CSV includes midline rows explicitly; an empty stratum is unavailable, never assigned a coverage percentage.</p>
<h2>Focus on sub-pixar123 and sub-pixar124</h2><div class="table"><table id="focused-counts"><thead><tr><th>Participant</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Region</th><th>Stratum</th><th>Included / total</th><th>Percent</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for r in rows %}{% if r.evidence != 'spm8_grid_2mm' %}<tr><td>{{ r.participant_id }}</td><td>{{ evidence_labels[r.evidence] }}</td><td>{{ r.region_id }}</td><td>{{ r.hemisphere }}</td><td>{% if r.evidence == 'spm8_full_atlas_2mm' %}{{ r.mask_voxels|int }}{% else %}{{ r.varying_voxels|int }}{% endif %} / {{ r.voxels|int }}</td><td>{% if r.voxels == 0 %}Unavailable{% elif r.evidence == 'spm8_full_atlas_2mm' %}{% if r.mask_unknown_voxels == 0 %}{{ '%.1f'|format(r.mask_fraction * 100) }}%{% else %}Unknown; see bounds{% endif %}{% else %}{{ '%.1f'|format(r.varying_fraction * 100) }}%{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<h2>How to interpret the asymmetry</h2><p>A whole-parcel average can be nonconstant even when only one side or a small boundary fraction supplies varying observations. These strata reveal where the measured support lies in the supplied normalized coordinates. They cannot identify whether acquisition coverage, masking, registration, template differences or distribution quantization caused a deficit. A temporal fluctuation can include residual artifacts. Do not treat a nonconstant average or a changed matrix as biological validation.</p>
<h2>Methods and exact denominators</h2><dl>{% for key,value in settings.items() %}<dt>{{ key }}</dt><dd>{{ value }}</dd>{% endfor %}</dl>
<h2>Verification and attribution</h2><p>The three stratum counts are reconciled with the sealed unsplit-region totals for every participant, region and evidence layer. An independent verifier uses Nilearn nearest-neighbor resampling and a separate coordinate formula to check all stratum counts. Original-frame counts, source SHA-256 values, finite BOLD values and valid mask membership are checked. Unknown mask values are preserved; lower and upper inclusion bounds are exported.</p>
<p>Source methods: <a href="https://s3.amazonaws.com/openneuro/ds000228/ds000228_R1.0.0/uncompressed/derivatives/README">SPM8/MATLAB archive</a> and <a href="https://osf.io/wjtyq/">fMRIPrep/tutorial methods</a>. Original study: Richardson et al. (2018), ds000228 R1.0.0. The historical SPM8 “fmriprep” folder is not the matching NiPrep fMRIPrep lineage. No additional source files were downloaded.</p>
